1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:04,297
Is your Millwater house due for its first repaint?

2
00:00:05,742 --> 00:00:07,575
Millwater went up in stages

3
00:00:07,611 --> 00:00:09,820
so whole streets have had the same number of summers on

4
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:10,571
their paint.

5
00:00:10,815 --> 00:00:13,547
A lot of homes here are reaching their first repaint at about

6
00:00:13,567 --> 00:00:14,588
the same time.

7
00:00:16,172 --> 00:00:18,098
On one Pioneer Rise repaint

8
00:00:18,134 --> 00:00:21,431
the weatherboard paint was flaking and blistering back to bare wood.

9
00:00:21,675 --> 00:00:24,333
The factory primer had failed when the house was built.

10
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:27,240
You can't paint over that.

11
00:00:27,426 --> 00:00:28,993
We sanded the whole house

12
00:00:29,063 --> 00:00:31,095
then sanded the flaked areas hard

13
00:00:31,165 --> 00:00:34,078
until only sound paint and bare weatherboard were left.

14
00:00:34,393 --> 00:00:36,644
Only then did the undercoat go on.

15
00:00:38,089 --> 00:00:41,606
That's why quotes for similar-looking houses can be so different.

16
00:00:41,746 --> 00:00:44,323
Ask every painter what prep is in the price.

17
00:00:45,709 --> 00:00:47,485
We're mh painting.

18
00:00:48,066 --> 00:00:50,775
Dulux Accredited, on the Hibiscus Coast.

19
00:00:50,795 --> 00:00:53,069
The full story is on our site.

